  "stories": [
    {
      "title": "Jensen Huang resigns at Nvidia.",
      "body": "Nvidia said at 8:48a Thursday that Jensen Huang resigned as president, CEO and director, effective immediately. CFO Colette Kress is interim CEO while staying CFO, former Synopsys CEO Harvey Jones becomes the board's first chair, and the search will weigh internal and external candidates. It follows WSJ and FT reports that the board met late Wednesday to consider removing him, after the NYT reported a second affair. NVDA was down 7.6% at $160.50 pre-market before the release (Wed close $173.73), while AMD (+2.3%) and Broadcom (+1.4%) rose. Earnings stay on Tue 11/17 after the close."
    },
    {
      "title": "December hike is the base case.",
      "body": "Tuesday's October CPI rose 0.4% (0.3% expected) and core 0.3% (0.2% expected), a third straight 0.3% core print; no year-on-year figure was published because October 2025 data was never collected during the shutdown. Waller backs a December hike and floated 50bp; Logan wants two more. Prediction markets price a 25bp hike at about 85% and 50bp at about 10%. Jobless claims rose to 200K Thursday (195K expected), still low. Next: October PPI Friday (+0.4% m/m expected) and a heavy Fed speaker slate.",
