    {
      "title": "Nebius beats, but the AI trade cools.",
      "body": "Nebius reported Q3 revenue of $980.8M (+571%), above the roughly $907M consensus, and a loss of $0.13 a share, narrower than expected, yet the stock fell 9–12% pre-market. CoreWeave, which jumped 24.7% Wednesday on its beat and raised 2026 guidance, was down about 7% pre-market, and Intel, Marvell and Micron fell 2.7–3.5%. Wednesday's rally had been led by semis (+5.6%)."
    },
    {
      "title": "Cisco and Applied Materials, Thursday after the close.",
      "body": "The next AI-infrastructure test, landing the day Nvidia's CEO resigned, with Cerebras also reporting after the close. Polymarket gives Applied Materials about a 71% chance of beating its $4.13 EPS estimate, down from 88% Wednesday. Morgan Stanley cut Cisco to Equal Weight going in."
    },
    {
      "title": "Anthropic IPO could trade as soon as Nov 19.",
      "body": "Anthropic set terms at $70–78 a share, raising up to $64.4B at a valuation of up to $1.4 trillion. CNBC's sources say it aims to start trading Thu Nov 19. Polymarket prices a listing by Nov 19 at about 81% and by Nov 30 at about 96%.",
      "odds": [
        {
          "source": "polymarket",
          "label": "Anthropic trading by Nov 19",
          "prob": 81,
          "slug": "will-anthropic-ipo-by-november-19-2026",
          "url": "https://polymarket.com/event/anthropic-ipo-by"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Oil: no more strikes, but Hormuz still bites.",
      "body": "Trump said further strikes on Iran aren't needed for now, but the US naval blockade stays and Iran says no talks are under way. Reports of tankers hitting mines in the Strait of Hormuz lifted crude early Wednesday; WTI settled up 0.4% at $86.42 and Brent was flat near $92.65, after Tuesday's 3.7% drop. Lower energy prices are what the inflation picture needs."
    }
